The Strandline Compact formalized Mafdet's coastal legal conversion regime during the Fracture Era.
It standardized how inland custody claims become maritime contract cargo at the coast.
In practice it works with dual-attestation doctrine: cargo legitimacy must survive both inland and harbor legal scrutiny.
The Compact became a cornerstone of intercity trust when overland records were contested or incomplete.
